# Website Performance Optimization - Complete Audit & Fix Prompt

## CONTEXT
I have a website with low performance (slow loading, poor user experience). I need you to analyze my code and implement ALL performance optimizations to achieve 90+ Lighthouse scores.

---

## YOUR TASK
Perform a complete performance audit and implement optimizations across ALL areas: images, code splitting, caching, bundle size, rendering, database queries, and more. Make the website FAST.

---

## STEP 1: INITIAL PERFORMANCE AUDIT

### 1.1 Run Lighthouse Audit
```bash
# Check current performance scores
npx lighthouse https://yourwebsite.com --view

# Or use Chrome DevTools:
# 1. Open Chrome DevTools (F12)
# 2. Go to "Lighthouse" tab
# 3. Click "Analyze page load"
# 4. Note scores for: Performance, Accessibility, Best Practices, SEO
```

### 1.2 Analyze Bundle Size
```bash
# Check current bundle size
npm run build
# Look for large bundles in build output

# Install bundle analyzer
npm install --save-dev @next/bundle-analyzer

# Add to next.config.js:
const withBundleAnalyzer = require('@next/bundle-analyzer')({
  enabled: process.env.ANALYZE === 'true',
})

module.exports = withBundleAnalyzer({
  // your existing config
})

# Run analysis
ANALYZE=true npm run build
```

### 1.3 Check Current Issues
Document current problems:
- [ ] Slow initial page load (> 3 seconds)
- [ ] Large JavaScript bundle (> 500KB)
- [ ] Unoptimized images
- [ ] No code splitting
- [ ] Slow database queries
- [ ] No caching strategy
- [ ] Layout shifts (CLS issues)
- [ ] Long tasks blocking main thread

---

## STEP 2: IMAGE OPTIMIZATION

### 2.1 Replace <img> with Next.js Image Component

**BEFORE (Bad):**
```jsx
<img src="/hero-banner.jpg" alt="Hero" width="1200" height="600" />
```

**AFTER (Good):**
```jsx
import Image from 'next/image'

<Image
  src="/hero-banner.jpg"
  alt="Hero"
  width={1200}
  height={600}
  priority // for above-fold images
  quality={85}
  placeholder="blur"
  blurDataURL="data:image/jpeg;base64,/9j/4AAQSkZJRg..." // tiny blur preview
/>
```

### 2.2 Optimize Image Formats

```bash
# Install sharp for automatic image optimization
npm install sharp

# Next.js will automatically:
# - Convert to WebP/AVIF
# - Resize to correct dimensions
# - Lazy load images below fold
# - Generate responsive srcset
```

### 2.3 Configure Next.js Image Optimization

```javascript
// next.config.js
module.exports = {
  images: {
    formats: ['image/avif', 'image/webp'],
    deviceSizes: [640, 750, 828, 1080, 1200, 1920, 2048, 3840],
    imageSizes: [16, 32, 48, 64, 96, 128, 256, 384],
    minimumCacheTTL: 60,
    domains: ['firebasestorage.googleapis.com'], // if using Firebase
  },
}
```

### 2.4 Lazy Load Images Below Fold

```jsx
// Images above the fold (visible immediately)
<Image src="/hero.jpg" priority />

// Images below the fold (lazy loaded)
<Image src="/gallery-1.jpg" loading="lazy" />
```

### 2.5 Add Blur Placeholders

```bash
# Install plaiceholder for blur placeholders
npm install plaiceholder

# Generate blur data URLs
import { getPlaiceholder } from 'plaiceholder'

export async function getStaticProps() {
  const { base64 } = await getPlaiceholder('/image.jpg')

  return {
    props: { blurDataURL: base64 }
  }
}

// Use in component
<Image
  src="/image.jpg"
  placeholder="blur"
  blurDataURL={blurDataURL}
/>
```

---

## STEP 3: CODE SPLITTING & LAZY LOADING

### 3.1 Dynamic Imports for Heavy Components

**BEFORE (Bad):**
```jsx
import HeavyChart from '@/components/HeavyChart'
import VideoPlayer from '@/components/VideoPlayer'

export default function Page() {
  return (
    <div>
      <HeavyChart data={data} />
      <VideoPlayer src="/video.mp4" />
    </div>
  )
}
```

**AFTER (Good):**
```jsx
import dynamic from 'next/dynamic'

// Lazy load heavy components
const HeavyChart = dynamic(() => import('@/components/HeavyChart'), {
  loading: () => <div className="animate-pulse h-64 bg-gray-200" />,
  ssr: false, // disable server-side rendering if not needed
})

const VideoPlayer = dynamic(() => import('@/components/VideoPlayer'), {
  loading: () => <div>Loading video...</div>,
})

export default function Page() {
  return (
    <div>
      <HeavyChart data={data} />
      <VideoPlayer src="/video.mp4" />
    </div>
  )
}
```

### 3.2 Conditional Lazy Loading

```jsx
'use client'

import { useState } from 'react'
import dynamic from 'next/dynamic'

// Only load when user clicks
const AdminDashboard = dynamic(() => import('@/components/AdminDashboard'))

export default function Page() {
  const [showDashboard, setShowDashboard] = useState(false)

  return (
    <div>
      <button onClick={() => setShowDashboard(true)}>
        Show Dashboard
      </button>

      {showDashboard && <AdminDashboard />}
    </div>
  )
}
```

### 3.3 Route-Based Code Splitting

```javascript
// Next.js automatically splits routes
// app/dashboard/page.tsx → separate bundle
// app/profile/page.tsx → separate bundle
// app/settings/page.tsx → separate bundle

// Each route only loads its own code
```

### 3.4 Optimize Third-Party Libraries

```jsx
// BEFORE: Import entire library
import _ from 'lodash'
import moment from 'moment'

// AFTER: Import only what you need
import debounce from 'lodash/debounce'
import groupBy from 'lodash/groupBy'
import { format } from 'date-fns' // lighter than moment

// Or use tree-shakeable alternatives
import { debounce } from 'lodash-es' // ES modules version
```

---

## STEP 4: BUNDLE SIZE REDUCTION

### 4.1 Remove Unused Dependencies

```bash
# Find unused dependencies
npx depcheck

# Remove them
npm uninstall unused-package-1 unused-package-2

# Check bundle impact
npm run build
```

### 4.2 Replace Heavy Libraries

```javascript
// REPLACE THESE HEAVY LIBRARIES:

// ❌ moment.js (288KB) → ✅ date-fns (13KB)
import moment from 'moment'
// Replace with:
import { format, parseISO } from 'date-fns'

// ❌ axios (40KB) → ✅ fetch (built-in)
import axios from 'axios'
// Replace with:
fetch('/api/data')

// ❌ lodash (71KB) → ✅ native JS
import _ from 'lodash'
// Replace with:
array.map(), array.filter(), etc.

// ❌ chart.js (200KB) → ✅ recharts (lighter) or victory
import Chart from 'chart.js'
// Replace with:
import { LineChart } from 'recharts'
```

### 4.3 Tree Shaking Configuration

```javascript
// next.config.js
module.exports = {
  webpack: (config, { isServer }) => {
    // Enable tree shaking
    config.optimization.usedExports = true
    config.optimization.sideEffects = false

    return config
  },
}

// package.json
{
  "sideEffects": false // enables tree shaking
}
```

### 4.4 Split Vendor Code

```javascript
// next.config.js
module.exports = {
  webpack: (config) => {
    config.optimization.splitChunks = {
      chunks: 'all',
      cacheGroups: {
        default: false,
        vendors: false,
        // Vendor chunk
        vendor: {
          name: 'vendor',
          chunks: 'all',
          test: /node_modules/,
          priority: 20
        },
        // Common chunk
        common: {
          name: 'common',
          minChunks: 2,
          chunks: 'async',
          priority: 10,
          reuseExistingChunk: true,
          enforce: true
        }
      }
    }
    return config
  }
}
```

---

## STEP 5: RENDERING OPTIMIZATION

### 5.1 Use React Server Components (Next.js 13+)

```tsx
// app/page.tsx - Server Component by default
async function getData() {
  const res = await fetch('https://api.example.com/data', {
    cache: 'force-cache' // or 'no-store' for real-time data
  })
  return res.json()
}

export default async function Page() {
  const data = await getData()

  return <div>{data.title}</div>
}
```

### 5.2 Optimize Client Components

```tsx
'use client' // Only add when needed

import { memo, useCallback, useMemo } from 'react'

// Memoize expensive components
const ExpensiveComponent = memo(function ExpensiveComponent({ data }) {
  // Component logic
  return <div>{/* ... */}</div>
})

// Memoize expensive calculations
function Component({ items }) {
  const sortedItems = useMemo(() => {
    return items.sort((a, b) => a.value - b.value)
  }, [items])

  const handleClick = useCallback(() => {
    // Handler logic
  }, [])

  return <ExpensiveComponent data={sortedItems} onClick={handleClick} />
}
```

### 5.3 Reduce Re-renders

```tsx
// BEFORE: Component re-renders on every parent render
function Child({ data }) {
  console.log('Rendering Child')
  return <div>{data.name}</div>
}

// AFTER: Only re-renders when data changes
const Child = memo(function Child({ data }) {
  console.log('Rendering Child')
  return <div>{data.name}</div>
})

// Or use React.memo with custom comparison
const Child = memo(
  function Child({ data }) {
    return <div>{data.name}</div>
  },
  (prevProps, nextProps) => {
    return prevProps.data.id === nextProps.data.id
  }
)
```

### 5.4 Virtualize Long Lists

```bash
npm install react-window
```

```tsx
import { FixedSizeList } from 'react-window'

// BEFORE: Renders all 10,000 items (slow!)
<div>
  {items.map(item => <Row key={item.id} data={item} />)}
</div>

// AFTER: Only renders visible items (fast!)
<FixedSizeList
  height={600}
  itemCount={items.length}
  itemSize={50}
  width="100%"
>
  {({ index, style }) => (
    <div style={style}>
      <Row data={items[index]} />
    </div>
  )}
</FixedSizeList>
```

---

## STEP 6: FONT OPTIMIZATION

### 6.1 Use Next.js Font Optimization

```tsx
// app/layout.tsx
import { Inter, Playfair_Display } from 'next/font/google'

const inter = Inter({ 
  subsets: ['latin'],
  display: 'swap',
  variable: '--font-inter',
})

const playfair = Playfair_Display({ 
  subsets: ['latin'],
  display: 'swap',
  variable: '--font-playfair',
})

export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en" className={`${inter.variable} ${playfair.variable}`}>
      <body className={inter.className}>{children}</body>
    </html>
  )
}
```

### 6.2 Preload Critical Fonts

```tsx
// app/layout.tsx
export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <html>
      <head>
        <link
          rel="preload"
          href="/fonts/my-font.woff2"
          as="font"
          type="font/woff2"
          crossOrigin="anonymous"
        />
      </head>
      <body>{children}</body>
    </html>
  )
}
```

### 6.3 Subset Fonts

```tsx
// Only load Latin characters (smaller file size)
const inter = Inter({ 
  subsets: ['latin'],
  // Remove: 'latin-ext', 'cyrillic', etc.
})
```

---

## STEP 7: CACHING STRATEGIES

### 7.1 Static Generation (SSG)

```tsx
// Generate at build time (fastest!)
export default async function Page() {
  const data = await fetch('https://api.example.com/data', {
    cache: 'force-cache' // Cache forever
  })

  return <div>{data.title}</div>
}

// With revalidation
export const revalidate = 3600 // Revalidate every hour

export default async function Page() {
  const data = await fetch('https://api.example.com/data', {
    next: { revalidate: 3600 }
  })

  return <div>{data.title}</div>
}
```

### 7.2 Client-Side Caching (SWR)

```bash
npm install swr
```

```tsx
'use client'

import useSWR from 'swr'

const fetcher = (url) => fetch(url).then((res) => res.json())

export default function Profile() {
  const { data, error, isLoading } = useSWR('/api/user', fetcher, {
    revalidateOnFocus: false,
    revalidateOnReconnect: false,
    dedupingInterval: 60000, // 1 minute
  })

  if (isLoading) return <div>Loading...</div>
  if (error) return <div>Error</div>

  return <div>Hello {data.name}!</div>
}
```

### 7.3 Browser Caching Headers

```javascript
// next.config.js
module.exports = {
  async headers() {
    return [
      {
        source: '/static/:path*',
        headers: [
          {
            key: 'Cache-Control',
            value: 'public, max-age=31536000, immutable',
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        source: '/images/:path*',
        headers: [
          {
            key: 'Cache-Control',
            value: 'public, max-age=31536000, immutable',
